 【63†Issues21 (21)】\nL121:   * 【64†Pull requests4 (4)】\nL122:   * 【65†Actions】\nL123:   * 【66†Projects】\nL124:   * 【67†Security and quality】\nL125:   * 【68†Insights】\nL126: \nL127: More items\nL128: \nL129: # perf(commit/extend): close the ~1.30× LDE gap vs native pil2 #58\nL130: \nL131: New issue\nL132: \nL133: Copy link\nL134: \nL135: New issue\nL136: \nL137: Copy link\nL138: \nL139: Closed\nL140: \nL141: 【69†Task】\nL142: \nL143: 【70†#62】\nL144: \nL145: Closed\nL146: \nL147: 【71†perf(commit/extend): close the ~1.30× LDE gap vs native pil2】#58\nL148: \nL149: Task\nL150: \nL151: 【70†#62】\nL152: \nL153: Copy link\nL154: \nL155: Labels\nL156: \nL157: 【72†enhancementNew feature or request】New feature or request\nL158: ## Description\nL159: \nL160: 【73†erkhesbold2005-blip】\nL161: \nL162: opened 【74†on Jul 9, 2026】\nL163: \nL164: Issue body actions\nL165: \nL166: ### Pre-submission checklist\nL167: \nL168:   * [Input] I have searched the existing issues and this is not a duplicate.\nL169: ### Context / problem\nL170: \nL171: Same-hardware measurement (RTX 5090, 2026-07-09) at real Main-air dims N=2^22 → N_ext=2^23 shows stage-1 `extend` (coset LDE, pil2's `extendPol`) is the largest remaining per-stage gap vs native pil2-stark:\nL172: \nL173: extend  | zisk-zorch  | native pil2  | ratio\nL174: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL175: cm1 (38 cols)  | 42.1 ms  | 32.5 ms  | 1.30×\nL176: cm2 (24 cols)  | 26.8 ms  | 20.4 ms  | 1.32×\nL177: Native from pil2-stark `bench_main_proof_gpu` (MAIN_LDE_CM1/CM2); zisk-zorch from `python -m zisk_zorch.bench_inner_proof --stages=extend`. The sibling `commit` stage was just closed from 1.19× → 1.04× via leaf-hash fusion (【75†#54】, merged), making `extend` the next bottleneck. `quotient`/`fri` have no clean native micro-bench baseline yet.\nL178: Root cause (hypothesis). `extend` (`zisk_zorch/commit/trace_commit.py:51-67`) runs `trace.T` → `lax.ntt(INTT)` → `rs.encode` (NTT) → `.T`. Both NTTs transform along the last axis (zorch `reed_solomon.py:197` NTTs `axis=-1`), so the two transposes of the 8M×38 matrix exist only to feed the NTT layout — two full-matrix DRAM round-trips. Native pil2 uses a tiled column-major NTT (`goldilocks_trace_layout.cuh`, \"column-major within tiles\") with no transpose.\nL179: Prime suspect = the transposes / row-major-vs-column-major layout; secondary = `lax.ntt` kernel quality vs pil2's sppark NTT.\nL180: ### Proposed solution\nL181: \nL182: Make the LDE column-native so the two transposes disappear:\nL183: \nL184:   * Add a column-axis (axis-0) NTT path to zorch `ReedSolomon.encode` / `lax.ntt` so the transform runs along the row axis without transposing; or\nL185:   * Keep the trace column-major end-to-end so `extend` output feeds the existing `column_major` leaf-hash commit path (zorch `merkle.py` already exposes a `column_major` option) with no transpose between extend and commit.\nL186: Confirm the attribution first (profile / HLO dump), then prototype the transpose-free path and measure. Likely a cross-repo change (zorch `ReedSolomon`, possibly the zkx NTT emitter), coordinated from this consumer repo.\nL187: ### Alternatives considered\nL188:   * Leave as-is / accept 1.30×. Rejected: extend is now the single biggest per-stage gap and directly gates end-to-end parity; commit is already at 1.04×.\nL189:   * Swap only the NTT kernel, keep the transposes. Rejected pending profiling: if the transposes dominate, a faster NTT alone won't close the gap — and the transposes may be forcing strided/slow NTT access in the first place. Profiling decides whether kernel-only suffices.\n"
